# ── PRODUCTION environment ────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this to .env for production deployments.
# Never commit .env to source control.

NODE_ENV=production

# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=8080
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Your production domain — used for CORS and sitemap
APP_URL=https://www.greenstreet.finance
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://www.greenstreet.finance,https://greenstreet.finance

# ── API authentication ────────────────────────────────────────
# verifyFirebaseToken (src/middleware/auth.ts) runs GLOBALLY on every /api/*
# route, but it only REJECTS unauthenticated requests when REQUIRE_AUTH=true.
# Left unset → the API is OPEN. That is currently REQUIRED for the app to work:
#   - The SPA never attaches a Firebase ID token to its fetch() calls (there is
#     no getIdToken() anywhere in src/), so even signed-in users send no
#     Authorization header. Firebase login is a client-side gate only.
#   - The DSCR Analyzer is reachable before login via "Try demo" (demoMode),
#     and /api/dscr/* is pure local compute with no external cost.
#
# DO NOT simply set REQUIRE_AUTH=true here. It is global, so it would 401 EVERY
# request — breaking the analyzer for demo AND signed-in users — until the
# frontend is changed to send `Authorization: Bearer <idToken>`.
#
# Open risk: /api/narrate calls a paid LLM (ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN) and is open,
# guarded only by IP rate-limiting (10/min, which resets on serverless cold
# start) = an API-key-abuse vector. The correct fix is PER-ROUTE auth on
# /api/narrate plus frontend token attachment — not this global flag.
# REQUIRE_AUTH=true   # enable ONLY after the SPA attaches Firebase ID tokens

# ── Anthropic ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# ── Firebase (VITE_ prefix → exposed to browser bundle) ───────
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ── Engine ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Number of worker_threads used to run DSCR solves in parallel. Set to 0 to
# disable worker_threads and run synchronously in-process — relevant to this
# Cloud Function's memory budget (see firebase.json / src/function.ts).
# Defaults to 4 for long-lived Node/Firebase hosts and 0 on Vercel.
# WORKER_POOL_SIZE=0
